%% title: Party Onboarding Flow
sequenceDiagram
  participant UI as admin-ui / mobile
  participant PS as party-service
  participant DB as PostgreSQL
  participant K as Kafka
  participant KYC as kyc-service
  participant AML as aml-service

  UI->>PS: POST /api/v1/parties (legal_name, email, partyType, …)
  PS->>DB: BEGIN TX
  PS->>DB: INSERT INTO parties (status=PENDING_KYC, kyc_status=NOT_STARTED, aml_status=NOT_SCREENED)
  PS->>DB: INSERT INTO party_outbox (PARTY_CREATED, status=PENDING)
  PS->>DB: COMMIT
  PS-->>UI: 201 Created {partyId}

  note over PS: OutboxDispatcher @Scheduled 5s
  PS->>K: publish PARTY_CREATED → openbank.party.events

  K-->>KYC: PARTY_CREATED (auto-open KYC case)
  K-->>AML: PARTY_CREATED (open CUSTOMER_ONBOARDING case)

  note over KYC: Checks: IDENTITY, ADDRESS, PEP_SCREENING, SANCTIONS_SCREENING, ADVERSE_MEDIA
  KYC->>K: KYC_CASE_APPROVED → openbank.kyc.events

  note over AML: Analyst four-eyes decision
  AML->>K: aml.case.status_changed.v1 (CLEARED) → openbank.aml.events

  K-->>PS: KYC_CASE_APPROVED consumed
  PS->>DB: UPDATE parties SET kyc_status=APPROVED

  K-->>PS: AML CLEARED consumed
  PS->>DB: UPDATE parties SET aml_status=CLEARED

  note over PS: deriveStatus(): kyc=APPROVED AND aml=CLEARED → ACTIVE
  PS->>DB: UPDATE parties SET status=ACTIVE
  PS->>DB: INSERT INTO party_outbox (PARTY_UPDATED)
  PS->>K: publish PARTY_UPDATED → openbank.party.events
